{"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/lowestcommonancestors"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LowestCommonAncestors","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"TreeAlgorithms"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"LowestCommonAncestors","externalID":"s:14TreeAlgorithms21LowestCommonAncestorsV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LowestCommonAncestors","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Lowest common ancestors of a rooted tree or arborescence, each in O(1) after O(n) work.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAncestors"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For vertices at preorder positions p < q, the answer is the vertex at the least position among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parents of the vertices at positions p + 1 … q. Those parents lie in the answer’s subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and include it, and it has the least position there. A query is therefore one range minimum"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over